s:538912:"{"quark-photofolio":{"name":"Quark Photofolio","version":"0.1.7","description":"A minimal, one-page photography portfolio theme built on the Quark 2 \/ Blades CSS foundation. Groups photos into sections, keeps the image itself the focus, opens a distraction-free fullscreen viewer on click, and automatically derives a web-sized thumbnail plus a watermarked full-size version from each upload.","description_html":"<p>A minimal, one-page photography portfolio theme built on the Quark 2 \/ Blades CSS foundation. Groups photos into sections, keeps the image itself the focus, opens a distraction-free fullscreen viewer on click, and automatically derives a web-sized thumbnail plus a watermarked full-size version from each upload.<\/p>","description_plain":"A minimal, one-page photography portfolio theme built on the Quark 2 \/ Blades CSS foundation. Groups photos into sections, keeps the image itself the focus, opens a distraction-free fullscreen viewer on click, and automatically derives a web-sized thumbnail plus a watermarked full-size version from each upload.","icon":"camera-retro","author":{"name":"Severin","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/severin10","email":"dietschiseverin@gmail.com"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","1.8","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/severin10\/grav-theme-quark-photofolio","keywords":"photofolio, photography, portfolio, one-page, onepager, gallery, lightbox, watermark, quark, dark, minimal","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/severin10\/grav-theme-quark-photofolio\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"0.1.7","date":"2026-08-25T05:56:04Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/quark-photofolio\/0.1.7","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/severin10\/grav-theme-quark-photofolio","slug":"quark-photofolio","install_path":"user\/themes\/quark-photofolio","content_sha256":"0b3623f2c80bf63088a36dc41d47cbe649f5816397061b008ff3fe9189a92f28","screenshot":"themes-quark-photofolio.jpg","changelog":{"0.1.7":{"date":"2026-08-25","content":"1. [](#new)\n   * `templates\/form.html.twig` \u2014 a standalone-page template for a page\n     modeled on Grav's own documented forms example (a `form.md` file with\n     a `form:` block, no theme-specific setup needed). It shows up in the\n     nav automatically, linking to its own URL.\n2. [](#improved)\n   * Nav now links a non-photo child page (like the new form page) to its\n     own URL instead of an in-page anchor; photo-section children keep\n     their `#anchor` links as before. Superseds 0.1.6's bubbled-form\n     dedup, which assumed the form would stay embedded in the one-pager.\n3. [](#bugfix)\n   * Removed the \"Contact\" placeholder slot from the footer\n     (`partials\/contact.html.twig`) \u2014 embedding a form inline in the\n     one-pager via Grav's child-to-parent form bubbling did not reliably\n     show it; a dedicated page (see above) is the documented, working\n     alternative. `partials\/support.html.twig` is unaffected.\n"},"0.1.6":{"date":"2026-08-25","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n   * Nav no longer hardcodes a \"Contact\" link unconditionally \u2014 if a\n     `contact`-slugged child page already provides one (e.g. a dedicated\n     form page, since Grav bubbles a child page's `form:` up to the\n     parent), that one is used instead of duplicating it\n"},"0.1.5":{"date":"2026-08-23","content":"1. [](#new)\n   * Fullscreen viewer: previous\/next navigation across all photos on the\n     page (wraps at both ends) \u2014 Left\/Right arrow keys, plus visible\n     chevron buttons either side of the photo title (just the two arrows,\n     with no gap between them, when a photo has no title). Hidden entirely\n     when the page only has one photo.\n"},"0.1.4":{"date":"2026-08-23","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n   * `.btn` background\/text color now fall back to guaranteed-defined\n     tokens (`--q2-text-strong` \/ `--q2-bg`) when no accent color is\n     configured, instead of an undefined `--q2-accent` that rendered as\n     an invisible\/transparent button \u2014 affected the form submit button and\n     any other `.btn` element\n   * JS assets are now only output once, at the very end of the page,\n     instead of also in `<head>` \u2014 a field's own script (e.g. the basic\n     captcha reload button) registers itself when that field renders,\n     which happens later, in the footer; the earlier `<head>` output call\n     could never have included it\n"},"0.1.3":{"date":"2026-08-23","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n   * Form submit\/reset buttons now get the theme's `.btn` class\n     (`form_button_classes`), so they render with real styling instead of a\n     bare, unstyled `<button>`\n"},"0.1.2":{"date":"2026-08-22","content":"1. [](#new)\n   * Reference implementation for the contact slot: `partials\/contact.html.twig`\n     renders whatever `form:` is defined on the current page via Grav's own\n     form plugin. Fully generic \u2014 no field list, spam-protection choice, or\n     recipient address lives in the theme; that stays in page content.\n"},"0.1.1":{"date":"2026-08-21","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * Contact and Support footer sections are now empty, optional include\n     slots (`partials\/contact.html.twig`, `partials\/support.html.twig`)\n     instead of hardcoded placeholder text\n"},"0.1.0":{"date":"2026-08-21","content":"1. [](#new)\n   * Initial release, forked from Quark 2"}}},"resume-nordic":{"name":"Nord Resume","version":"1.0.0","description":"A modern resume theme.","description_html":"<p>A modern resume theme.<\/p>","description_plain":"A modern resume theme.","icon":"user-secret","author":{"name":"Gy\u00f6ngy\u00f6si G\u00e1bor","email":"gyongyosigabor@gshoots.hu"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.0"},{"name":"error"},{"name":"problems"}],"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/megvadulthangya\/grav-theme-resume-nordic","demo":"https:\/\/nordic-skeleton.gshoots.hu","license":"MIT","tag_name":"v1.0.1","date":"2025-12-20T19:33:31Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/resume-nordic\/1.0.0","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/megvadulthangya\/grav-theme-resume-nordic","slug":"resume-nordic","install_path":"user\/themes\/resume-nordic","content_sha256":"2abcccb0b4c7480dd8043a4f5ac903851cbe7b43764b9bc398e9b696d96a9448","screenshot":"themes-resume-nordic.jpg","changelog":{"1.0.1":{"date":"12\/20\/2025","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed missing description text in Education and Experience templates\n    * Fixed text visibility issues in Light Mode (removed hardcoded colors)\n    * Fixed rating dots rendering in the second column of Skills module\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Switched Experience section to full-width layout for better readability\n    * Improved mobile responsiveness for timeline items\n"},"1.0.0":{"date":"12\/15\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **Initial Release of Nord Resume**\n    * Complete rebranding to \"Nord Resume\" (slug: `resume-nordic`)\n    * Implemented **Nord Color Palette** with automatic Dark\/Light mode detection\n    * Replaced legacy Foundation Icons with local **FontAwesome 7.1.0** assets\n    * Added **Admin Panel Configuration** (blueprints):\n        * Toggle Gravatar & adjust size\n        * Custom footer text\n        * Toggle credits\n    * Refactored templates to remove hardcoded personal data\n    * Fixed HTML rendering in Experience and Interests descriptions\n    * Optimized CSS for better icon alignment (Flexbox)"}}},"quark2":{"name":"Quark 2","version":"1.1.16","description":"The modernized Grav default theme \u2014 Blades CSS foundation, Cal.com-inspired aesthetic, with light\/dark\/auto mode and Font Awesome 7 icons.","description_html":"<p>The modernized Grav default theme \u2014 Blades CSS foundation, Cal.com-inspired aesthetic, with light\/dark\/auto mode and Font Awesome 7 icons.<\/p>","description_plain":"The modernized Grav default theme \u2014 Blades CSS foundation, Cal.com-inspired aesthetic, with light\/dark\/auto mode and Font Awesome 7 icons.","icon":"meteor","author":{"name":"Team Grav","url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org","email":"devs@getgrav.org"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=2.1.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["2.1"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2","keywords":"quark2, blades, pico, theme, core, modern, fast, responsive, html5, dark-mode","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"1.1.16","date":"2026-10-02T01:18:43Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/quark2\/1.1.16","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2","slug":"quark2","install_path":"user\/themes\/quark2","content_sha256":"fff88a4f50b9f02e8ce4c826184fa7972fef4581a56814239d11df361b1179c3","screenshot":"themes-quark2.jpg","changelog":{"1.1.16":{"date":"10\/01\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The 404 and other error pages now sit in the same white content card as regular pages. Thanks @Mikanoshi and @Jah-yee [#26](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/26)\n    * The \"Back home\" button on error pages can now be translated instead of always showing English. Thanks @Mikanoshi [#26](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/26)\n"},"1.1.15":{"date":"09\/28\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * You can now upload your own favicon (PNG, SVG or ICO) in the theme settings, next to the custom logos. Thanks @abesnier [#25](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/pull\/25)\n"},"1.1.14":{"date":"09\/15\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Spanish is now available as a site language. Thanks @pmoreno-rodriguez [#24](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/pull\/24)\n"},"1.1.13":{"date":"09\/11\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Meta tag content was escaped twice, so a description containing `&` or a space showed up as `&amp;amp;` and `&#x20;` in the page source. The theme's copy of the metadata partial is gone and Grav core's is used instead, which also adds the `<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text\/markdown\">` tag for Grav 2.1's Markdown output\n1. [](#improved)\n    * The theme now requires Grav 2.1.0 or later\n    * The sidebar's feed links use Grav 2.1's format-aware page URLs, so a blog at the site root links to `\/index.rss` and `\/index.atom` instead of working around the home route by hand\n"},"1.1.12":{"date":"09\/09\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Icons chosen in the admin now render. The icon picker saves a value with the `fa-` prefix already on it, and the templates added a second one, so a changed icon silently disappeared while the ones shipped with a skeleton kept working. Feature, menu and page icons all accept whatever form the value arrives in. Thanks to @UnixxSH [getgrav\/grav-skeleton-onepage-site#20](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-skeleton-onepage-site\/issues\/20)\n"},"1.1.11":{"date":"08\/13\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The appearance toggle's tooltip and screen-reader label are now translatable, instead of always appearing in English ([#23](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/23))\n    * Every other screen-reader label in the theme, covering the menus, breadcrumbs, pagination and post navigation, is now translatable too\n"},"1.1.10":{"date":"08\/04\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Dropdown menus near the right edge of the window no longer run off-screen, and nested sub-menus now open toward whichever side has room ([#22](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/22))\n    * Removed the stray horizontal scrollbar that off-screen dropdown panels were adding to every page\n    * The theme no longer ships a rule that kept custom logos out of your site's git repository ([#21](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/21))\n"},"1.1.9":{"date":"08\/02\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The active menu item is no longer white-on-white in dark mode while the header sits over a hero\n    * Removed a hairline of page background that showed above the hero in light mode before scrolling\n"},"1.1.8":{"date":"08\/02\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Restored the `header-dark` and `header-light` body classes from the original Quark theme, so you can pick a readable header colour when it sits over a hero image\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * The `header-transparent` option now actually lets the hero show through the header, instead of only clearing the header's own background ([#21](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/21))\n    * The Features module's `Layout` option now controls the column count as its description says, giving 4 \/ 3 \/ 2 columns for Small and 3 \/ 2 \/ 1 for Standard ([#20](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/pull\/20))\n"},"1.1.7":{"date":"07\/30\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Forum Pro's own headings now use Cal Sans along with the rest of the theme. The forum falls back to the body font when a theme hands it no display face, which left a forum page title looking lighter than the headings sitting under it\n"},"1.1.6":{"date":"07\/20\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Restored the full set of hero classes from the original Quark theme, so `hero-fullscreen`, the hero size options, `text-light`\/`text-dark`, `title-h1h2`, and the image overlays all work again ([#18](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/18)).\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * The hero background parallax effect now works again; it was lost when the theme was rebuilt for Grav 2.0 ([#17](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/17)).\n"},"1.1.5":{"date":"07\/17\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Tag lists now respect an optional `filterend` limit so you can cap how many tags are shown ([#219](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark\/issues\/219))\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * The `image_align: left` option on modular text sections now moves the image to the left instead of leaving it on the right ([#16](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/16))\n"},"1.1.4":{"date":"07\/14\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The login plugin's admin-style panels now follow dark mode instead of staying light, so the login, forgot, and reset forms match the rest of the theme in dark mode ([#14](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark2\/issues\/14))\n"},"1.1.3":{"date":"07\/09\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Custom SVG logos are now inlined so they follow light and dark mode like the built-in logo, instead of staying a fixed color\n"},"1.1.2":{"date":"06\/24\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Pagination buttons no longer show list-item markers\n    * On-page menu items now highlight as active on modular pages\n"},"1.1.1":{"date":"06\/12\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Headings and body text now read their fonts from CSS variables, so the display and sans-serif fonts can be changed from custom.css without editing the theme\n"},"1.1.0":{"date":"06\/01\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Moved the theme's CSS foundation to Blades CSS, the actively maintained successor to the now-dormant Pico CSS, with no change to the look or layout\n    * Added a small npm build so the CSS base can be refreshed with `npm install && npm run build` instead of swapping files by hand\n    * Tightened the spacing inside dropdown menus so longer menus stay compact and no longer run off the bottom of the screen\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the PHP Debug Bar message text being unreadable in light mode\n    * Fixed the third-level dropdown menu sitting slightly too high next to the item that opens it\n"},"1.0.5":{"date":"05\/28\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Restored the oklab color-mixing across the theme that was temporarily switched to sRGB in 1.0.4 \u2014 links, accents, focus rings, alert backgrounds, and hero gradients are back to their original tints\n1. [](#new)\n    * Added two Twig helpers, `q2_mix_white(hex, pct)` and `q2_mix_alpha(hex, pct)`, that return pre-resolved `rgb()` \/ `rgba()` strings for sites that need to feed third-party widgets a color value their parser can understand\n    * Documented an optional `#disqus_thread` override block in the README for sites running Disqus via JSComments, where the embed's older color parser cannot read modern `color-mix()` results in dark mode\n"},"1.0.4":{"date":"05\/27\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed Disqus comments failing to load when a page is opened directly in dark mode\n1. [](#improved)\n    * Form tabs now have a visible active state in dark mode and use a clean underlined nav style\n    * Form toggles now match input field height and use the configured accent color for the selected option\n    * Form submit and reset buttons no longer stretch the full container width and use a readable foreground color against the accent background\n    * Form checkboxes and radios now pick up the configured accent color and have consistent sizing across light and dark modes\n    * Form basic captcha now uses the theme palette, the verification image fills the field vertically, and the reload button is always visible\n    * Form file upload (Dropzone) now renders with dark mode colors and a muted action button instead of an accent-styled pill\n    * Form Filepond uploader panels, labels, and item action buttons now use the theme palette in dark mode\n"},"1.0.3":{"date":"05\/17\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added admin blueprints for the `default`, `blog`, `item`, and `modular` page templates so every option is now editable from the admin panel\n    * Added admin blueprints for the `hero`, `features`, `text`, and `gallery` modular sub-templates\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed pagination rendering as empty on blog listings when the Pagination plugin is enabled\n    * Fixed the sticky header flickering between its full and collapsed sizes when scrolled to right around the trigger point\n    * Fixed a 500 error that could occur when a custom logo value was left in a malformed or empty state, now falls back to the default Grav logo\n"}}},"anonymous":{"name":"Anonymous","version":"1.0.5","description":"A cyberpunk\/matrix-inspired theme for Grav CMS with privacy-focused aesthetics","description_html":"<p>A cyberpunk\/matrix-inspired theme for Grav CMS with privacy-focused aesthetics<\/p>","description_plain":"A cyberpunk\/matrix-inspired theme for Grav CMS with privacy-focused aesthetics","icon":"terminal","author":{"name":"Kusai Mara","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Kusaimara"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.0"}],"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/Kusaimara\/grav-theme-anonymous","demo":"https:\/\/grav-demo.kusaimara.net","keywords":"grav, theme, cyberpunk, privacy, matrix, hacker, security, anonymous","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/Kusaimara\/grav-theme-anonymous\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"Ver-1.05","date":"2026-06-25T04:45:36Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/anonymous\/1.0.5","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/Kusaimara\/grav-theme-anonymous","slug":"anonymous","install_path":"user\/themes\/anonymous","content_sha256":"920feb866dacfc9ab84f9ac9b7aa26f19db1c545251d0864f00b5b586e48d64d","screenshot":"themes-anonymous.jpg","changelog":{"Changelog":{"date":"2026-06-23","content":"### Fixed\n- Added the SEO \/ Social (Open Graph image) tab to the `blog` page template as well\n  (it was previously only on `item` and `default`, so blog-type pages did not show it)\n\n### Note\n- Theme blueprint changes require a cache clear (`bin\/grav clear-cache`) to appear in Admin\n- New pages must be saved once before the media upload area becomes available (Grav default)\n\n## [1.0.4] - 2026-06-23\n\n### Added\n- Per-page Open Graph image: og:image \/ twitter:image now resolve in priority order\n  page-selected image > page featured image (first media) > site-wide theme default\n- \"SEO \/ Social\" tab on page and post editors with an Open Graph image picker\n  (`filepicker` from the page's own media) for choosing a dedicated share image\n\n## [1.0.3] - 2026-06-23\n\n### Added\n- Blog listing template (`blog.html.twig`) with a responsive post-card grid and pagination\n- Single post template (`item.html.twig`) with featured image, tags\/date\/author meta,\n  previous\/next navigation and back-to-blog link\n- Blog list works out of the box from published child pages; a defined `content.items`\n  collection in the page header is used automatically when present (enables pagination)\n\n## [1.0.2] - 2026-06-23\n\n### Fixed\n- Fixed logo \/ Social Share Image \/ favicon upload in Theme settings showing a\n  \"Value theme:\/\/images\/...\" error and failing to upload\n- Removed hard-coded file paths that were pre-seeding the `file` fields with\n  unresolved values (root cause of the upload error)\n- Made og:image, twitter:image and favicon resolution array-aware (file fields\n  store the uploaded value as an array keyed by path) and skip the tags when unset\n- Added the missing `images\/` folder so the `theme:\/\/images` upload destination exists\n\n## [1.0.1] - 2025-11-08\n\n### Improved\n- Enhanced text readability for blog posts and content pages\n- Increased font size from 14px to 16px for better readability\n- Improved text color from #888 to #bbbbbb for better contrast\n- Enhanced line height from 1.6 to 1.9 for comfortable reading\n- Added green color to list markers for better visual hierarchy\n- Improved heading spacing and margins\n- Enhanced link visibility with bold font weight\n- Better code block and inline code styling\n- Improved table hover effects\n- Enhanced blockquote styling\n- Better mobile responsiveness for text content\n\n### Fixed\n- Fixed H2 heading positioning with proper top margins\n- Fixed list item indentation and positioning\n- Corrected nested list spacing\n\n## [1.0.0] - 2025-10-14\n\n### Added\n- Initial release of Anonymous theme\n- Cyberpunk-style design with matrix rain effects\n- Glitch text animations\n- Terminal-inspired aesthetics\n- Responsive design for all devices\n- Custom form styling\n- Theme configuration via YAML\n- Support for Open Graph and Twitter Card meta tags\n- Customizable color scheme via CSS variables\n\n### Features\n- Matrix rain background effect (toggleable)\n- Glitch effect on headers (toggleable)\n- Mobile-responsive navigation\n- Optimized for performance\n- No external tracking"}}},"applenotes":{"name":"Apple Notes","version":"1.1.0","description":"Port of Apple Notes Theme from alanagoyal","description_html":"<p>Port of Apple Notes Theme from alanagoyal<\/p>","description_plain":"Port of Apple Notes Theme from alanagoyal","icon":"rebel","author":{"name":"Paul Massendari","email":"paulmassendari@pm.me"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.6.0"},{"name":"tntsearch","version":">=3.0.0"}],"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-theme-apple-notes","demo":"https:\/\/notes.paulmassendari.dev","keywords":"grav, theme, etc","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-theme-apple-notes\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"v1.1.0","date":"2026-01-26T15:49:25Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/applenotes\/1.1.0","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-theme-applenotes","slug":"applenotes","install_path":"user\/themes\/applenotes","content_sha256":"ce3a0260f98c55b150729b4964795120fb88043b8dd978fd64017e910b65eb7e","screenshot":"themes-applenotes.jpg","changelog":{"1.0.0":{"date":" 12\/04\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started...\n    * Initial Release"}}},"kahuna":{"name":"Kahuna","version":"1.0.12","description":"The KahunaCart storefront theme \u2014 sand, koa and lagoon, one hand-written stylesheet, light and dark from one token block, and every brand decision a custom property away.","description_html":"<p>The KahunaCart storefront theme \u2014 sand, koa and lagoon, one hand-written stylesheet, light and dark from one token block, and every brand decision a custom property away.<\/p>","description_plain":"The KahunaCart storefront theme \u2014 sand, koa and lagoon, one hand-written stylesheet, light and dark from one token block, and every brand decision a custom property away.","icon":"shopping-bag","author":{"name":"Trilby Media, LLC","url":"https:\/\/trilby.media","email":"hello@trilby.media"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=2.0.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/kahunacart\/grav-theme-kahuna","demo":"https:\/\/kahunacart.com","keywords":"kahuna, kahunacart, commerce, ecommerce, shop, storefront, store, theme, responsive, dark-mode","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/kahunacart\/grav-theme-kahuna\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"1.0.12","date":"2026-10-04T18:23:35Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/kahuna\/1.0.12","repository":"https:\/\/kahunacart.com","premium":{"vendor":"KahunaCart","validator":"kahunacart","license_product":"kahunacart","checkout_url":"https:\/\/kahunacart.com\/shop\/product\/kahunacart","button":"Buy Now","filename":"grav-theme-kahuna"},"slug":"kahuna","install_path":"user\/themes\/kahuna","content_sha256":"940e192460f251783600cd1a0b88aef6773b7f23ac2c11a06a4784b3f1e4637e","changelog":{"1.0.12":{"date":"10\/04\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **A currency switcher in the header.** With KahunaCart 1.4.0, a store that sells in more than one currency gets KahunaCart's currency menu in the header beside the cart and the appearance control, drawn as the same kind of pill with a list that opens like the account menu, and as a labelled \"Currency\" row in the mobile menu on a phone, where the header's own row has no room. It opens and closes with no JavaScript, a click away or Escape closes it, and it is drawn in light and dark from the theme's own colours. Nothing is drawn on a store with one currency, and on a KahunaCart older than 1.4.0 the theme is as it was\n    * **\"Not available in EUR\" where a price would be.** A product nobody priced in the shopper's currency shows the plugin's own line in place of its price on a product tile, a hero card, the home page's fanned cards and the product page, where the page's buy box says it with a link back to the store's own currency. There is no price, no sale flag and no stock line beside it, and no add button. A price that is missing is never drawn as free or as a sale\n    * **The shopper's currency stays on their links.** Product, category, shop and search links in the tiles, hero cards, home page, header, footer and the \"Back to shop\" links carry `?currency=EUR` for a shopper who is not in the store's own currency, and the live search box carries it as a field, so what they browse next stays in their currency and a shared cache can keep it\n    * **Checkout says why there is no way to pay.** When a store has payment methods and none of them takes the order's currency, the payment step says so in the theme's warning notice, using KahunaCart 1.4.0's new `providers_excluded_currency` page variable, instead of an empty list\n    * **The notice a currency switch leaves behind is seen.** Switching an open cart's currency says what was repriced and what was taken out. The notice is drawn on the shop's pages as before, and now on the home page and ordinary pages too, which have no messages area of their own, but only on a store with a currency switcher. The currency question page (\"Your cart would be empty\") is the theme's own too, in the page title, callout and button the rest of the theme uses\n    * **An open cart explains why a currency link did not change its prices.** Product, category, search and listing pages draw KahunaCart's cart-currency notice with the theme's notice styling and a button to switch the cart. An unavailable product uses the same switch button when the cart holds its currency, and a cart held at a payment provider offers no switch. A store with one currency gets neither notice nor button\n2. [](#improved)\n    * **Sale-tier amounts in the cart are in the cart's currency.** The cart's \"buy 3 and pay\" hint printed its fixed amounts in the visitor's currency rather than the cart's, which only differs on a store that sells in more than one. The overrides of the product page, product grid, hero section, category page, search page and search box are now stamped `@version 1.4.0`, and `tests\/check-currency.php` renders the tiles, hero cards, product page, home page and header to check the unavailable states, the links, the switcher and which templates may print a price without naming a currency\n    * **The storefront overrides follow KahunaCart's latest 1.4.0 fixes.** Cart and bundle forms, receipt and refusal links, and the checkout's back links keep the shopper's currency. Back-in-stock forms inherit core's currency field, and the delivery step names the currency when no shipping method is priced in it\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * **A hosted payment offers a fresh cart in the wanted currency.** Product, category, search, listing, cart and checkout pages inherit KahunaCart\u2019s private restart notice, with one signed POST button styled for phones and the chosen appearance\n    * Checkout keeps coupon and delivery refusals in its own messages block so they remain visible after an AJAX update\n    * Choosing \u201cDeliver instead\u201d after collection with JavaScript off clears the previous delivery method and asks for a fresh choice before payment\n    * **Checkout explains payment fees with JavaScript off.** Choosing a method updates the fee, tax and total with KahunaCart\u2019s checkout script, and the page explains the extra charge when scripting is off\n    * **Site navigation keeps a currency chosen in the URL.** Home, About, Journal, Bookings, brand, sign-in and account links keep the explicit choice, while cookie-only navigation and single-currency links stay plain\n    * **The cart explains its currency lock.** Following another currency now shows the new-cart explanation on the cart page, and cancelling a payment permits changes to its items rather than its currency\n    * **Narrow shop, category and search pages stay within the viewport.** Hidden filter legends keep their one-pixel width instead of stretching beyond the sidebar\n    * **The currency switcher looks the same on every page.** The theme now styles the whole menu without needing KahunaCart's shop stylesheet, including the summary, floating list and form buttons, in light and dark and in the mobile menu. With JavaScript off the mobile menu stays open so its Currency row can still be used\n    * **Checkout offers no payment choices or Place order button when no method takes the cart's currency.** The warning explains why there is no way to pay instead of asking the shopper to choose a method that does not exist\n    * **Collection satisfies the checkout's delivery step.** While a collection point is selected, the theme hides and disables the alternative delivery methods so they cannot hold Continue to payment or Place order disabled. Choosing delivery again restores them on the next response, and returning from Continue keeps the unused delivery address hidden\n    * **Currency flash notices reach every page using the theme's base template.** Blog and booking templates supplied by another plugin now inherit the notice block too, and the message queue is read once\n"},"1.0.11":{"date":"09\/30\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **Paywalled articles look like Kahuna articles.** With KahunaCart 1.3.8, a page marked `paywall:` shows a visitor who can't read it the teaser and a subscribe panel instead of the article. The theme's new `kahunacart-paywall.html.twig` draws that page in the same column as any other page here, with the hero header, the prose style and the panel drawn as one of the theme's cards, in light and dark and down to phone width. A page with no hero fields gets its title as the heading, unless the teaser opens with a heading of its own. The override is stamped `@version 1.3.8` and never prints the page's body. Readers see the page's normal template as before, and the free-article bar and the reader's wide tables and code blocks sit in the article's column the way they do on any page\n    * **The receipt says \"Continue reading\" after a customer subscribes from an article.** The receipt override draws KahunaCart 1.3.8's Continue reading button above the order number, linking back to the article the customer was reading, and the override is now stamped `@version 1.3.8`. It draws nothing for anyone else, and nothing on an older KahunaCart\n"},"1.0.10":{"date":"09\/29\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **Receipt downloads use the file's title.** With KahunaCart 1.3.6 a product file can carry a title, and the receipt override now names each download by it, falling back to the file name as before, and prints the file's description under it when it has one. The override is stamped `@version 1.3.6`\n    * **The current account tab keeps its look when it is a link.** With KahunaCart 1.3.6, an add-on's tab stays linked on the pages below it (a licence key's own page links back to Licenses), and it is drawn in the same highlight as the current tab\n    * **The receipt's closing links say what they are.** View invoice, Your orders, Back to shop and \"Sign in to manage your purchases\" carry the same `kahunacart-order-link` classes as KahunaCart 1.3.6's own receipt (`--invoice`, `--orders`, `--shop`, `--signin`), and the arrow on Back to shop is its own element, so a child theme can draw them as buttons with icons. They look the same as before\n"},"1.0.9":{"date":"09\/28\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **The product page shows the product safety details the EU asks for.** Under the custom fields there is now a closed **Product safety** section: the manufacturer with its address, email and website, the responsible person in the EU when the manufacturer is outside it, and the product's safety information. It is drawn by KahunaCart 1.3.5's new `partials\/kahunacart-product-safety.html.twig`, styled to sit with the custom fields and the tags, and it shows nothing on a product with no manufacturer and no safety text, or on an older KahunaCart without the partial. The override is stamped `@version 1.3.5`. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n    * **Energy labels and other product labels, near the price.** With KahunaCart 1.3.5, the product page draws a product's labels under the lead price: the EU energy class arrow in its class's colour with its \"Product information sheet\" link beside it, and label images such as a warranty badge. Each opens the full label in the plugin's lightbox, and a label for one variant shows only while that variant is picked. Product tiles, and the hero section's cards, draw the energy arrow under their price too, outside the tile's own link so it opens the label rather than the product. The buy button is told not to draw the labels a second time. With an older KahunaCart nothing changes. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n    * **Product pictures open full size.** With KahunaCart 1.3.5, a click on a product page's picture opens the product's pictures as a set in the plugin's lightbox, with arrow keys and swipe between them, and shows the pictures as they were, with no link, when the store has turned **Open Gallery Pictures in a Lightbox** off. A product with one picture opens it the same way. Videos and embeds are left as they are. The product page, the product grid and the hero section overrides are stamped `@version 1.3.5`, and `tests\/check-product-labels.php` renders them to check all of it, including that an older plugin still gets the page it always had. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n    * **\"Notify me when it's back\" looks at home on the product page.** KahunaCart 1.3.5 offers a back-in-stock email under the buy button wherever the chosen variant can't be bought: one button that toggles for a signed-in customer, an email field for a guest. The theme's product page gets it through the plugin's buy button, as one quiet panel flush under the buy box in the theme's surface, radius and input style, with \"We'll email you when it's back\" in the in-stock green. The account area's new **Stock alerts** tab draws each alert as a card like the address cards. Nothing changes with an older KahunaCart. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n2. [](#improved)\n    * **The theme's script and stylesheets carry a version.** `kahuna.js`, `kahuna.css`, `custom.css` and `fonts.css` were loaded without one, so after an update a browser could keep the old script beside the new templates it was written for. Each is now loaded with its modification time on the end (\"?v=\u2026\"), so any change to the file makes browsers fetch it fresh. On a site that turns on Grav's own **Enable asset timestamp**, Grav stamps the files it manages itself and the theme leaves them alone\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * **A link to one variant opens the product page on it.** The page always opened on the default variant, whatever the plugin chose, so a `?variant=` link (the back-in-stock email's, or a product feed's) showed the default's price and stock line. It now opens on the plugin's own choice, and on the default variant with a plugin that sends none\n    * **The stock line follows the variant picker.** The \"In stock\" line under the lead price was drawn for the variant the page opened on and never changed, so picking a size that had sold out still said \"In stock\" (the buy button below it knew better). Every variant's line is now drawn into the page from one new partial, `partials\/stock-line.html.twig`, and swapped in as the picker moves, the same way the lead price follows it: \"Out of stock\", \"Only a few left \u2014 3\", the variant's backorder note or \"In stock\"\n    * **Tax inside the prices is said to be included once.** The shipping and tax estimate read \"VAT (19% incl.) (included)\", because KahunaCart's tax line already says \"incl.\" and the estimate added \"(included)\" after it. It now adds it only to an included line whose label doesn't say so, such as one from a tax add-on. It reads the flag KahunaCart 1.3.5 puts on the line rather than looking for the English \"incl.\", so it works in every language\n"},"1.0.8":{"date":"09\/26\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **The receipt shows the customer's VAT number and the reverse-charge line.** An order the store entered by hand with a customer VAT ID, or with **Don't charge tax** (KahunaCart 1.3.4), prints them under the totals, and the answers to the store's checkout fields print there too. Orders placed in the shop look the same as before. The override is stamped `@version 1.3.4`. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n    * **Prices can say whether they include tax.** With KahunaCart 1.3.4's **Say whether prices include tax** switched on, the product page prints \"incl. VAT\" or \"excl. VAT\" under the lead price, and product cards, the home page's featured tiles and hero section cards print it under theirs, in the theme's quiet muted style (`.k-price-note`). The buy button on the product page is told not to say it a second time. With the setting off, or on an older KahunaCart, nothing changes. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n    * **The product page shows the product's custom fields.** The public custom fields a merchant fills in on a product (a warranty, a country of origin) now appear after the specification table, where the plugin's own product page puts them, laid out like the facts under the buy box. Internal fields are never shown\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * **Checkout draws every field the store declares.** The checkout drew its own fixed set of inputs, so fields added under KahunaCart \u2192 Checkout \u2192 Fields (a VAT number, say), the company line once it was switched on, and fields from add-ons such as the newsletter opt-in never appeared, and a field the merchant turned off, relabelled or reordered stayed as it was. It now draws the plugin's checkout field model section by section, through a Kahuna-styled override of `partials\/kahunacart-checkout-field.html.twig`, so a field is shown, required or hidden exactly as the store's rules say for the address the shopper has entered. The address lines keep their autocomplete hints. With a KahunaCart older than 1.2.0, which has no field model, the checkout draws the fields it always did. Asked for by a merchant in the EU\n"},"1.0.7":{"date":"09\/26\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **Backorders say so.** KahunaCart 1.3.3 tells the shopper when a variant is out of stock but still for sale. The product page's stock line shows the variant's backorder note, the store's wording or \"On backorder\" in the warning colour, a product card carries the same words as a small badge where the low-stock line goes, and cart, checkout and receipt lines print \"2 of 3 on backorder \u00b7 Expected to ship late October\" under the line. The plugin's own note beside the buy button is hidden on the product page, because the stock line already says it. With an older KahunaCart the cart, checkout, receipt and card print nothing new\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * **A tracked variant at zero with backorders allowed no longer says \"In stock\".** The stock line checked sold out, then low stock (which needs at least one left), and fell through to \"In stock\" for a variant with none. This holds with an older KahunaCart too: a tracked variant at zero that is not sold out says \"On backorder\" in the theme's own words\n"},"1.0.6":{"date":"09\/23\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **The shop's front page carries the store's structured data.** KahunaCart 1.3.0 describes the store itself to search engines and AI shopping agents (name, logo, support contact and return policy) on the shop's front page. The theme's product listing now includes the partial that prints it, as its category page already did. Nothing is printed with an older KahunaCart or with agentic commerce switched off.\n"},"1.0.5":{"date":"09\/21\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **Checkout draws the store's payment methods.** A store that set up payment methods in KahunaCart (**Payment methods** \u2014 \"Credit or debit card\", \"PayPal\", \"Bank transfer\", each with its own label, order, description and fee) still saw the bare provider radios in this theme, because its checkout predated methods: the merchant's labels and order never reached the page. It now draws the methods in the merchant's order, as the theme's own choice cards, with the description underneath and a fee on the right, and posts `payment_method` so the plugin names the provider. A method a condition rules out is drawn disabled with its reason (\"available on orders over \u00a3500\"); one unavailable for any other reason \u2014 store credit a guest does not hold, a gateway this basket cannot use \u2014 is left out rather than shown as \"Temporarily unavailable\". A store with no methods sees the provider radios exactly as before\n    * **The account page's customer group badges sit tight under the customer's name.** KahunaCart 1.2.11 shows the groups a customer is in as badges on the account and profile pages; the name line's own bottom margin is taken off when the badges follow it, so the two read as one block\n    * **The cart and checkout show KahunaCart's bundle notice.** With bundle suggestions turned on, a basket holding every part of a cheaper bundle gets a notice above the cart and at the top of checkout saying what the parts come to and what the bundle costs, with **Swap to the bundle** and **Keep them separate**. Keep them separate answers in place without reloading the page. Needs KahunaCart 1.2.11.\n\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * **A cart line whose quantity an add-on decided no longer offers a box.** A stay, a hire or a booking priced by an add-on is one thing, and KahunaCart has always refused a change to its quantity with a sentence naming the line \u2014 but the cart drew a number box beside it anyway, so a guest typed 2, pressed **Update cart**, and was told off for doing what the page had just invited them to do. The number is printed instead, on the same right edge and in the same figures, and the Remove button is still there because removing such a line is always allowed. An ordinary line keeps its box. This reads KahunaCart 1.2.11's `kahunacart_line_fixed_qty()`, so this release of the theme wants that version of the plugin.\n    * **A part-paid order's badge is amber instead of plain.** The receipt badges the payment status by name, and **part paid** \u2014 the status a customer sits at between paying a deposit and paying the balance \u2014 had no colour of its own, so it came out in the bare badge shape while every other status beside it was tinted. It sits with *awaiting payment* now, for the same reason: money is still owed on the order. The words themselves come from KahunaCart 1.2.11, which is where the missing string was.\n    * **A service is no longer badged \"Digital download\".** The badge and the Kind row on the product page asked whether a product ships, and a haircut ships no more than a PDF does. They ask what the product's type sells now: KahunaCart 1.2.11 answers that as the type's `nature`, and on an older KahunaCart the type's own code stands in. A booking says \"Booking\" in the Kind row and carries no download badge.\n    * **A download that has run out no longer says \"Sold out\".** The badge on a listing tile and the stock line on the product page printed the theme's own \"Sold out\" for anything at zero stock, which reads oddly for a file. Both now print KahunaCart 1.2.11's `kahunacart_stock()` label: \"Out of stock\" for something that ships, and for a download whatever the store picked under **Settings \u2192 Stock** (\"Not available\" by default, or \"Coming soon\"). The \"Only a few left\" line follows the store's own low-stock threshold instead of a fixed five.\n    * **A link in a KahunaCart notice or cart line note is a link.** KahunaCart 1.2.11 lets a notice say \"Sign in to the account that holds your license\" with Sign in as a link, and lets a line note carry one too. The cart and checkout print line notes through `|kahunacart_message`, and a link in a notice takes the notice's own ink with an underline, like the theme's other inline links\n"},"1.0.4":{"date":"09\/16\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **The button on a listing card reads \"View details\".** \"View\" on its own does not say where it takes you. The theme restates KahunaCart's own `VIEW_PRODUCT` string in its language file rather than editing the plugin, so every listing button the plugin draws picks up the longer wording.\n    * **A link styled as a button is the theme's filled pill now, the same as a real button beside it.** KahunaCart ships a fallback button style for themes that have none, and it loads after this stylesheet, so a plain `.button` rule lost the tie anywhere inside a storefront section. \"Add to cart\" escaped it \u2014 it is a `<button>`, and the theme names the element \u2014 but \"View details\" on a listing card is a link, so it came out in the plugin's small outlined box right next to the theme's pill. Every button style here names the link as well now, so the two match.\n    * **A table written in a page keeps its first column on one line.** A markdown table is nearly always a name and an explanation, and automatic table layout hands the width to whichever column asks for more \u2014 so the column of names was squeezed into a strip about one word wide while the sentences beside it took everything else, and \"KahunaCart Subscriptions\" came down the page a word at a time. The first cell of every row holds its words on one line now, which asks for the width the longest name actually needs and leaves the rest to the explanation. On a phone the table itself is the scroll port, the way the plugin's cart and order tables already are at that width, so a table too wide for the screen moves sideways on its own instead of dragging the page with it, and the columns after the first hold a readable measure there rather than taking whatever the names left over.\n    * **The sale badge on a big listing card sits with the prices now instead of centred on a line of its own.** A store that groups its listing into sections draws the top of it as large cards \u2014 picture on the left, the text on the right \u2014 and the campaign's badge landed on its own line under the price, centred, with the title and the summary above it hard left. It reads the way the product page reads now: the sale price, the old price struck through, then the campaign's name, all on one line against the left edge, wrapping onto a second line when the card is narrow. The theme carries its own copy of the plugin's hero partial to do it.\n\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * **The express-pay block sits in the checkout column now, not across the top of the page.** A store with a wallet button installed opened its checkout with \"Express checkout\" centred over a black button stretched from one side of the window to the other and \"or continue below\" under it, sitting above the two columns \u2014 a banner over the page rather than one of the two ways to pay. The block moved inside the left column, above the first numbered section: the caption in the same small muted weight as a field label, the buttons on the same left edge as the inputs and capped so a lone wallet button is a button rather than a bar, and \"or continue below\" set into the theme's own hairline. The first section keeps its bare top under it, so there is one line between the two and not two. Nothing renders on a store with no express provider, exactly as before. The same change went into KahunaCart 1.2.10's own checkout\n    * **An express-pay button reads on the dark side of the theme.** The wallet button drew itself in the flat colour the store's `express.theme` setting named \u2014 black, by default \u2014 so on the dark palette it was a near-black slab on a near-black page with a black label on it, present but invisible. KahunaCart 1.2.10 makes `auto` the default and lets the theme say what `auto` looks like, and this theme says koa with sand lettering on the light side and sand with koa lettering on the dark one: the same pair every other surface on the page swaps, so the button follows the Colour Scheme option and the system preference along with everything else. A store that wants its wallet buttons in some other colour sets `--kahunacart-express-auto-bg` and `--kahunacart-express-auto-fg` on `.kahunacart-express` in `css\/custom.css`, and a merchant who picked dark, light or outline outright still gets that flat colour on both sides\n    * **A delivery method the carrier would not quote for no longer shows a price beside the refusal.** A carrier-bound method a courier declined kept whatever placeholder cost was sitting beside the binding \u2014 nearly always zero \u2014 and the checkout printed it, so a shopper read \"FedEx Priority Overnight \u00b7 $0.00 \u00b7 No rate is available for this order right now\" next to a radio button nobody could press. The refusal stands on its own now, and a method the cart can actually have still says what it costs. The same change went into KahunaCart 1.2.10's own picker\n"},"1.0.3":{"date":"09\/15\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **The Country and State selects look like the boxes beside them.** A select is the one control in a form the browser still draws itself, and on macOS it drew a shorter box in its own grey, ignoring the background, the border and the corner radius this theme had set on it \u2014 so two controls in the middle of the billing address sat half a centimetre short of their neighbours in a colour from nowhere. They are the theme's own box now, same height, padding, ground, border, radius and type as a text box, with the theme's chevron at the end of them and a palette of its own on the dark side. The state select the plugin swaps in when the country changes is the same control and gets the same treatment.\n    * **The line saying what a greyed-out button is waiting for has a place of its own under every button.** The plugin's script draws that line where a theme has not put an element for it, and the one it made in the summary panel landed on top of Place order. Both Continues and Place order now carry their own, so the line always appears in the same place \u2014 just under the button, with an info glyph in front of it, small but in reading ink rather than a caption grey.\n    * **Picking a delivery method now changes the total in the summary panel.** The radios were read on the next submit and nowhere else, so a shopper who clicked a faster service went on looking at the cheaper one's price beside **Place order**, with the button live over a figure that was no longer true. KahunaCart 1.2.9 stores the choice the moment it is made and re-renders checkout, and it puts two regions of the answer back on the page \u2014 the delivery step, and the summary panel, which needs `id=\"kahunacart-checkout-summary\"` on it for that. Both fade and stop taking clicks while the request is out. With scripting off nothing changed: the radios are read by the next submit, which is the checkout that has always worked\n    * **Unticking \u201cShip to the billing address\u201d shows the delivery fields where you unticked it.** The fieldset was drawn only on a page that already knew the answer, so a shopper unticked the box, looked at the same form, and had to press Continue and wait for a page load before there was anywhere to type. It is on the page from the first paint now, carrying `hidden` while the box is ticked, and KahunaCart 1.2.9's checkout script takes the attribute off the moment the box changes \u2014 the theme carries `data-kc-ship-same` on the box and `data-kc-ship-to` on the fieldset for it. Their required flags come off `checkout_sections` as before, so Continue greys out again and names the delivery fields as they appear, and the delivery options reprice for the new destination a moment later. With scripting off nothing changed: untick, press Continue, and the page comes back with the fieldset open\n    * **A greyed-out button now says \u201cChoose a delivery method\u201d and \u201cChoose a payment method\u201d** rather than pointing at the heading over the list. KahunaCart reads `data-kc-choice-label` off the step or the fieldset to name a choice in the words a shopper would use, and this theme's delivery step and payment fieldset carried neither, so both read \u201cChoose an option under \u2026\u201d instead\n\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * **Checkout no longer lets Continue through with the state empty after the country changes.** The state field is rebuilt by the browser when the country changes, and the theme was passing the plugin the answer for one country rather than for all of them \u2014 so a shopper whose password manager filled in United States got a select with nothing insisting on it. The theme hands the plugin's own per-country answer through now, which is what KahunaCart 1.2.9 publishes it for.\n    * **Place order works again on a checkout with \u201cShip to the billing address\u201d ticked.** The delivery-address fieldset is drawn on every page now and hidden while the box is ticked, and its required fields keep their `required` flags \u2014 so the browser refused the submit over a field it could not show the shopper and had nowhere to put the cursor. The two Continue buttons carry `formnovalidate` and never met it; **Place order** does not, so pressing it did nothing at all, with only \u201cAn invalid form control with name='shipping_address1' is not focusable\u201d in the console to say why. The hidden fieldset is `disabled` as well as `hidden` now, and KahunaCart 1.2.9's script takes both attributes off together\n"},"1.0.2":{"date":"09\/15\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * **Checkout is a flow now, with a button under each part of it.** KahunaCart 1.2.9 splits checkout into three steps \u2014 the address, the delivery method, the payment \u2014 and this theme overrides the checkout template, so it carries the whole arrangement across: a wrapper around each step, a Continue at the end of each numbered section, and Place order beside the totals saying the one thing it does instead of changing its wording as the page moved along. Each button posts which step it came from, so \"please choose a delivery method\" arrives as the next step rather than as an error under a button that did what it said. With JavaScript running, a Continue stays greyed out until the fields above it are answered and the delivery options appear on their own a moment after the address is complete \u2014 no press, no page load. With scripting off nothing is lost: every button is live, and the first Continue brings back the page with the options on it, which is what checkout has always done\n    * **The delivery options are the theme's own markup whether they arrive with the page or a moment later.** They live in `partials\/kahunacart-checkout-shipping-step.html.twig` now, a theme override of the plugin's step partial, because that same file is what the plugin returns when the script asks for the options on their own \u2014 leave it to the plugin and every one of those swaps would paste the plugin's reference markup over this theme's picker. Collection points come with it, drawn in the theme's own choice rows; this theme has never drawn them before, so a store offering counter collection showed its customers nothing\n    * **The address fields say which ones the customer has to answer.** The plugin works that out \u2014 the destination country's own post-office rules, what the payment platform needs, whatever the merchant marked required \u2014 and the theme reads the answer off `checkout_sections` rather than guessing. A US address now insists on the state, an order of downloads asks for no street at all, and the Continue button waits for exactly the fields the server is going to check. The theme marked none of them required before, so a shopper could press Continue on an empty address and get a refusal back\n    * A chevron after each Continue caption, pointing at the section it takes you to, and an id on each step \u2014 `kahunacart-checkout-address`, `-shipping`, `-payment` \u2014 so a Continue can land on the step below rather than at the top of the page\n\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * **The checkout opened on whichever payment provider happened to load first, whatever the store had set as its default.** The picker pre-selected `loop.first`, so a store that configured Stripe as its default watched every customer arrive on Bank Transfer \u2014 the base plugin's own method always registers before any add-on. It follows `checkout.default_provider` now, the same way KahunaCart's own checkout does\n    * **A shipping method priced by a live carrier no longer shows as 0.00 at checkout.** This theme overrides the checkout template, and its delivery picker looped `shipping.methods` and printed each method's `cost_minor` \u2014 the number stored on the method row, which for a carrier-priced method is zero, because the real price is the rate the courier just quoted. So a customer picked \"DHL Express \u2014 0.00\" and then watched the order summary beside it charge them the actual rate. The picker now loops `shipping_offers`, the same list core's own partial uses, and prints each offer's `price_minor`, which is the price on the order either way. Methods this basket cannot have come with it: they are drawn disabled, carrying the sentence that says why \u2014 over the weight limit, under the free-shipping minimum \u2014 where before they were simply missing and a customer had no idea the option existed. Nothing changes on a store with no carrier driver, where an offer's price is its method's cost\n    * **The delivery picker no longer prints a line of machine data under a method's name.** A carrier's rate carried both the sentence a shopper reads and the codes a label is bought with, all on one map, and this picker prints that map by looping it \u2014 so a method priced by a live carrier came with `demo cached driftwood_ground Driftwood Ground 1215 USD 5 domestic 6000 1 1 demo_rate_8e6c5d` under its own name. KahunaCart 1.2.9 splits the two, and the picker prints only the half a person reads. It also draws the one sentence KahunaCart makes out of the other half \u2014 \"Arrives tomorrow\", \"Arrives in about 5 days\" \u2014 when the carrier said how long it would take. On an older KahunaCart nothing at all is drawn there\n    * **A carrier's own reason for refusing a delivery service is what the shopper reads now.** A driver that will not take a parcel says why in its own words \u2014 \"this service will not take a parcel over 900 mm on its longest side\" \u2014 and KahunaCart keeps that sentence on the offer, in `reason_params.detail_key`, beside its own generic one. The picker printed the generic one, \"the carrier cannot send this order by this service\", which tells a shopper nothing they can act on while the sentence that would have helped sat unread in the offer. The driver's sentence is printed when there is one, and KahunaCart's own when there is not\n"},"1.0.1":{"date":"09\/12\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **The receipt carries KahunaCart's purchase block for analytics.** KahunaCart 1.2.7 puts the order on the confirmation page as one JSON block, with no personal data in it, and a script that fires `kahunacart:purchase` for GA4, Google Tag Manager, Plausible or Meta snippets. This theme overrides that template, so it now draws the block too; on an older KahunaCart nothing is drawn\n"},"1.0.0":{"date":"09\/08\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **The fonts are served from the theme, not from Google.** Albert Sans, Bricolage Grotesque and Spline Sans Mono now ship as variable woff2 files under `fonts\/` with their own `css\/fonts.css`, so a storefront makes no request to fonts.googleapis.com and its type cannot change under it when a CDN does. The `display_font` toggle still turns them off in favour of the system stack.\n    * The cart's order summary shows one line per sale rather than one per discounted item. A quantity-tier campaign covering six lines writes six adjustments, all carrying the same label, and the summary panel was printing \"Bundle and save\" six times with six small numbers under it \u2014 six offers, to read it, rather than the one that is actually running. The panel now hands the plugin's `summary_adjustments` to the totals partial, which is the same rows with each sale collapsed to a single line carrying the whole saving and everything else left where it was. It falls back to `adjustments` on a plugin version that does not offer it\n\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * **The cart never drew the Cancel this payment button, so a frozen cart had no way out.** When a shopper leaves a payment page open at the provider, KahunaCart freezes the cart \u2014 the amount on that page was fixed when it was created and nothing in the cart can change it \u2014 and tells the shopper to finish the payment or cancel it. The plugin's own cart draws the notice and the button; this theme's override drew neither, so every store on this theme showed a shopper a cart that would not change, with no explanation and no button, on a page that quietly ignored Update cart. The notice is now here in the theme's own warning treatment, with the button under it\n    * **The express-pay zones were missing from the cart and the checkout**, so a store that installed a wallet add-on got no wallet buttons and no error to explain it \u2014 the zones render nothing when nothing is mounted in them, which is exactly why the absence was invisible. Both `cart.express` and `checkout.express` are drawn now, in the same places the plugin's own templates put them: under the cart's actions, and above the checkout's address form so a wallet carrying its own address can skip the form\n    * The cart template carries an `@version` stamp again, so `bin\/plugin kahunacart templates:drift` stops reporting it as an override of unknown age. It was the drift report that would have caught both bugs above. The theme's other twelve overrides are still unstamped and still on that list\n\n1. [](#new)\n    * KahunaCart's catalogue pagination, in the theme's listing. The results region draws the plugin's pager after the grid, so paging goes through the same swapped fragment a filter change does and needs no JavaScript of its own, and the product count above the grid now reads the whole result set rather than the rows on the page \u2014 \"24 products\" over page 1 of 108 was the wrong number\n    * KahunaCart's quantity-tier sales \u2014 \"buy 2, save 10%\" \u2014 throughout the storefront. A tile whose only campaign is a ladder says \"Buy 2+ and save\" instead of striking a price through against a discount that is not there yet, the product page leads with the regular price and lets the ladder under the buy button make the case, and the cart gains a brand-tinted panel above the totals saying which rung is in force and what one more item would do. All three read the plugin's new `has_discount`, so a campaign that does take money off a single purchase is drawn exactly as it was\n    * The SKU in the product facts follows the resolved variant through the picker's `data-kc-sku` hook\n    * Styling for the facet counts that follow the filters: `is-disabled` on a value nothing reachable answers, dimmed and struck out of the tab order by the `disabled` the panel puts on its input; `kahunacart-filter-none`, the muted italic line a facet with nothing reachable in it collapses to; and `is-unavailable` on a category branch holding nothing, dimmed on the row rather than the item so a dead subtree does not fade twice over. All of it is colour and opacity in the theme's own palette; the states themselves come from the plugin\n    * Styling for KahunaCart's two new catalogue pieces: `kahunacart-attribute-link`, the specification-table value that links to the rest of the catalogue answering it, drawn as ink with a dotted rule that fills in on hover rather than as a second colour running down the table; and `kahunacart-filter-more`, the Show all disclosure under a facet the store's value cap has shortened, styled like the panel's Clear link because it reveals rather than does\n    * First release \u2014 a storefront-first Grav 2.0 theme for KahunaCart\n    * The cart's estimate box, in the theme's own markup: KahunaCart's \"estimate shipping & tax\" block sits in the summary column as a panel of its own, with the country select, the state and postcode fields the store's zones actually need, and the estimated lines as a hairline-ruled list. Picking a country swaps the box in place through htmx \u2014 the same vendored copy live search already loads, pointed at `hx-post` on the cart route and `#kahunacart-estimate` as the target \u2014 and with JavaScript off it is the plain form post it always was. A store that charges nothing shows a price of nothing: the quiet \"we do not deliver there\" line is kept for an address the store's zones genuinely do not reach\n    * A visitor-facing colour scheme control in the header \u2014 light, dark, auto \u2014 with the choice kept in `localStorage` and stamped on `<html>` by a tiny inline script in the head, so a returning visitor never sees a frame of the wrong palette. `auto` is a real third state, stored by forgetting the key, so somebody who changes their mind follows their operating system again for good. The new `scheme_toggle` option hides it, and it hides itself when `color_scheme` pins the store to light or dark \u2014 that option is the store owner deciding, and a toggle beside it would be an argument the page cannot win. The control sits with the cart on a wide screen and moves into the menu panel on a phone\n    * Live product search. KahunaCart answers `{shop}\/search` with the results region alone for a request carrying `HX-Request: true`, and the theme's search form now asks for exactly that: typing swaps the grid in place from the first keystroke, on the shop as well as the search page, with the URL following through `hx-push-url` so a live result is still a link that can be sent and reached with the back button. Clearing the box puts every product back. htmx is vendored in `js\/vendor\/` and enqueued only by the two pages that use it \u2014 no CDN, and no 50KB on a category page. With JavaScript off every attribute is inert and the form submits the way it always did\n    * Flash messages are drawn by the theme now. `partials\/messages.html.twig` overrides Grav's own, which is the path the Login plugin's sign-in, forgot-password, reset, magic-link, registration and profile pages all include \u2014 so \"Login failed\" arrives as an alert box in the theme's own language, with a mark, a colour and a `role=\"alert\"`, instead of a line of unstyled text in the corner of the page. On a sign-in page it is laid out over the card it is answering rather than across the container. KahunaCart's own message partial is given the same treatment, so a storefront has one vocabulary for the same event\n    * An article layout for ordinary markdown pages: the measure is centred in the container instead of pinned to its left edge, and tables and code blocks lean out past it on a wide screen. Markdown tables, lists and headings are styled \u2014 a table written in a page had no class to give it and so had no styling at all. The storefront templates and the marketing `home` template are untouched\n    * A theme override of the plugin's `kahunacart-product-grid` partial, so every grid the plugin draws \u2014 search results included \u2014 uses the theme's own tile rather than the plugin's reference card\n    * KahunaCart's own identity as the default: salt and sand grounds, koa ink, lagoon as the brand colour and board as the action colour, Bricolage Grotesque for headings with Albert Sans and Spline Sans Mono alongside, and the microbus mark shipped in `images\/` for the header and footer lockup\n    * Two brand tokens split by job \u2014 `--k-brand` for identity (links, current states, selected options, emphasis) and `--k-accent` for action (buttons, the cart count, the lead price, the tinted word in the store name) \u2014 with every derived colour following from them, so a site rebrands in two lines of `custom.css`\n    * One palette written with `light-dark()`: the system preference decides by default and the new `color_scheme` option pins the store to light or dark through `data-theme` on `<html>`. Browsers without `light-dark()` get the light palette\n    * A storefront home page template (`home`): hero with the store's own products fanned out beside the copy \u2014 the three newest, or any three pinned by slug with `hero_products`, each showing its real picture when it has one \u2014 or a page image, department strip from `kahunacart_categories()`, featured grid with a lead tile from `kahunacart_products()`, and a facts list \u2014 all driven by the page header, none of it in the theme\n    * KahunaCart's automatic sales, in the theme's own furniture. A campaign covering a variant sets the price on the tile, in the hero stack and beside the product title, strikes the regular price next to it and puts the campaign's own name in the badge \u2014 \"Autumn sale\", not a generic word \u2014 while the compare-at price is left undrawn, because a claim about what something costs today beats a claim about what it used to cost. The lead price on a product page follows the option picker: pick a different waist and the sale price, the struck regular price and the badge all change with it, copied from the strings KahunaCart already formatted in the buy form rather than recomputed here. The \"On sale\" facet the plugin adds to the catalog rail while a campaign is running needed no work \u2014 it is the same control the in-stock checkbox is \u2014 and a sale's discount arrives in the cart summary as its own line, the way a coupon's does\n    * Product tiles with no box: picture, name, price, two lines of summary, and a flag for sale, sold out or digital on the picture. The whole tile is the link and the \"View\" button is gone\n    * Monogram tiles for products without a picture, kept to a warm band of hues so a grid of them reads as one catalog\n    * Header re-laid as brand, page links, controls \u2014 the links on the centre line, the cart and account on the right, the menu button with them on a phone. Sign-in moves into the menu panel on a phone\n    * Announcement bar above the header (`announcement` option), a footer with the brand, the departments, the account pages and the site's pages over a koa ground with the board rule across the top, and a branded 404\n    * Listing masthead with the product count and the search form beside the title; the catalog rail as a column of typography with hairlines rather than panels, sticky on wide screens\n    * Numbered checkout sections with hairlines instead of boxes, the order summary as a sunk panel; the product page with a sticky gallery, a facts list (kind, SKU, variant count) and the description in a two-column band\n    * The account area laid out with a rail \u2014 the section links down the left, the page on the right \u2014 through theme rules scoped under the `.kahuna` body class, since the pages are the plugin's own\n    * Theme options for the brand colour, the tinted word (`brand_tint`), an uploaded `logo` that replaces the lockup and doubles as the favicon, the colour scheme, and the announcement\n    * A film of grain over the page, tinted shadows, pill buttons with hover and pressed states, focus rings on the brand colour, and `--k-radius-btn` for sites that want square ones\n    * `partials\/brand.html.twig` shared by the header and footer; `fonts` and `announcement` blocks in the base template for child themes\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * The catalog tree's disclosure markers lined up with nothing. The browser's own `<details>` marker is laid out outside the summary's box at a width the platform picks, and a leaf row has no marker at all \u2014 so at three depths no two labels shared a left edge and the indent guides ran through the middle of things. Every row is built the same way now: a fixed slot for the chevron, empty on a leaf, then the label. The guide is drawn down the centre of the parent's chevron and stops on the last child instead of dangling past it, and the chevron turns when the branch opens\n    * Every storefront link the theme drew broke on a Grav installed in a subdirectory: the header cart link, the shop link in the navigation and the footer, the home page's department strip and CTA, the product cards and the 404's \"browse the shop\" all built their URLs from KahunaCart's base *route*, which starts at the site root and so pointed one folder too high. They are built from the plugin's new `kahunacart_url()` now; the navigation still compares `uri.path` against the route, which is what a route is for. `tests\/check-storefront-links.php` keeps it that way\n    * The plugin's link-style buttons (the address \"Delete\", \"Use for billing\") were painted as filled accent buttons by the theme's bare `button[type=\"submit\"]` rule; the rule now leaves any button with a class of its own alone\n    * Account menu in the header: an avatar button opening the customer's account pages \u2014 including the credentials page, whose slug is read from the plugin rather than assumed \u2014 and a sign-out link, with a sign-in link shown to visitors who are signed out. The avatar is the customer's own picture where the store has one and a generated one otherwise, both supplied by the plugin. `show_account_menu` turns it off\n    * Styles the Login plugin's sign-in form, which ships a hardcoded near-white card and no text colour of its own \u2014 on this theme's dark palette its heading and labels were light ink on a light card\n    * The order receipt renders panels contributed by other plugins through `onKahunaCartOrderPanels`, so a licence key or booking reference from another plugin still reaches the customer even though this theme overrides that template\n    * `templates\/partials\/base.html.twig`, the template every KahunaCart storefront page extends, providing the `content` and `head` blocks the plugin's templates fill\n    * Theme overrides of `kahunacart-products`, `kahunacart-category`, `kahunacart-product`, `kahunacart-cart`, `kahunacart-checkout`, `kahunacart-order`, `kahunacart-processing`, and `kahunacart-denied`\n    * KahunaCart integration is a custom-property hand-off first: the theme publishes `--kahunacart-*` override hooks (plus the generic `--grav-*` and `--theme-accent` tokens) mapped onto its own palette, and the plugin's `assets\/kahunacart.css` styles the storefront markup. No plugin partial is forked \u2014 buy button, catalog sidebar, subcategory cards, breadcrumbs, tags, coupon form, totals, and flash messages are all included from the plugin. Two blocks the theme lays out rather than merely spaces \u2014 the product gallery and the catalog sidebar \u2014 do carry theme rules against `kahunacart-*` classes, every one scoped under a `k-*` ancestor\n    * Product cards render the primary image KahunaCart attaches to every listed product \u2014 the plugin's cropped derivative, with intrinsic width and height so a grid never reflows as the pictures land \u2014 and fall back to a monogram tile tinted from the product id when a product has no picture\n    * Product pages render the plugin's full gallery: a scroll-snapping row of images with in-page thumbnail links, no JavaScript, styled through the theme's own `k-gallery-*` classes alongside the plugin's\n    * Storefront structured data and canonical link included from the plugin's `kahunacart-seo` and `kahunacart-seo-head` partials, on product and category pages and nowhere else\n    * Storefront search form on the product listing, so `{route}\/search` is reachable by navigation\n    * Cart table that reflows into labelled cards below 640px; checkout laid out as form plus sticky order summary, with the account prefill and \"save this address\" checkbox the plugin offers logged-in customers\n    * Header cart badge via `kahunacart_cart_count()`\n    * Light and dark palettes driven by `prefers-color-scheme`, both built from a single `--k-accent` token\n    * Theme options for brand name, tagline, accent color, display font, sticky header, cart link, category nav, grid columns, and footer text\n    * One stylesheet, no build step; the only JavaScript is the mobile nav toggle\n    * Checkout override carries the plugin's full form contract: ISO country selects (billing and delivery), the delivery-address fieldset when \"ship to billing\" is unticked, and repopulation of every field after a refused submit\n    * Descriptions and offline payment instructions render through the plugin's `kahunacart_markdown` filter, which escapes raw HTML instead of passing it through\n    * Checkout offers the plugin's create-account opt-in to guests when store accounts are enabled\n    * Checkout includes the plugin's address-suggestion panel so the optional address validation can offer its close match\n    * Catalog sidebar on the product listing and on category pages: the plugin's category tree and facet panel included whole, in a two-column layout that only exists when there is a sidebar to put in it. `catalog_nav` is null on a store with no categories and no applicable facets, and the templates then emit no wrapper, no aside and not one extra element \u2014 the flat listing renders exactly as it did before any of this existed\n    * The tree and the facet panel wear the theme's own panel: bordered, filled, shadowed, with the header nav's hover fill and accent tint on the current category, and the browser's real `<details>` disclosure marker left in place. No JavaScript\n    * Category pages render the department landing page \u2014 the plugin's subcategory cards, restyled to match the theme's product cards down to the 4:3 tile and the lift on hover \u2014 plus the category banner image and the ancestor breadcrumb trail\n    * Breadcrumbs on category and product pages, from the plugin's partial. On a product they replace the plain \"back to shop\" link, whose destination is already the trail's first crumb, and the link comes back for a product filed nowhere\n    * Product pages show the product's tags as outlined pills \u2014 deliberately not the theme's filled badge and not the category rows in the rail, because a tag links into a filtered listing rather than to a place in the catalog\n    * Filter-aware listings: the \"nothing matches those filters\" message with a clear-filters link, and the plugin's truncated-result notice\n    * Below 52rem the sidebar stops being a sidebar and sits above the listing, full width, with a full-width Apply button \u2014 a customer who has just tapped a department wants the subcategory links and the filters before the grid, not after fifty product cards\n    * The category chips are gone, replaced by the tree. `show_category_nav` is retained and does nothing, so an existing site's saved config stays valid"}}},"helios":{"name":"Helios","version":"2.1.17","description":"A modern, highly configurable documentation theme built on Tailwind CSS 4 and Alpine.js","description_html":"<p>A modern, highly configurable documentation theme built on Tailwind CSS 4 and Alpine.js<\/p>","description_plain":"A modern, highly configurable documentation theme built on Tailwind CSS 4 and Alpine.js","icon":"book-open","author":{"name":"Trilby Media, LLC","email":"hello@trilby.media"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.6"},{"name":"svg-icons","version":">=1.0.0"},{"name":"shortcode-core","version":">=4.0.0"},{"name":"simplesearch","version":">=2.0.0"},{"name":"codesh","version":">=1.0.0"},{"name":"page-toc","version":">=1.0.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/helios","docs":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/helios\/docs","demo":"https:\/\/demo.getgrav.org\/helios\/","keywords":"grav, theme, documentation, tailwind, docs, api, premium","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/labels\/helios","license":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/license","tag_name":"2.1.17","date":"2026-08-27T13:40:06Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/helios\/2.1.17","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/trilbymedia\/grav-theme-helios","premium":{"permalink":"grav-premium-helios","validator":"local","checkout_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/helios","button":"Buy Now","filename":"grav-theme-helios"},"slug":"helios","install_path":"user\/themes\/helios","content_sha256":"96a70fb9ad5b765d2affc23edaa51e606d1e6f9b4030c275095224179f8d6b2c","screenshot":"themes-helios.jpg","changelog":{"2.1.17":{"date":"08\/27\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Form buttons now have a proper style out of the box. Any form built with the Forms plugin rendered its Submit and Reset buttons as plain invisible text unless the page happened to add its own classes ([getgrav\/grav-premium-issues#617](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/617)).\n"},"2.1.16":{"date":"08\/11\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The file tree shortcode keeps its line breaks and indentation when you switch to Editor Pro and back, instead of being flattened onto one line ([getgrav\/grav-premium-issues#614](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/614)).\n"},"2.1.15":{"date":"07\/17\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the PHP debug bar not rendering (and its \"PhpDebugBar is not defined\" console error) by outputting the default `head` JS asset group, which core and plugins use and the theme was previously dropping\n"},"2.1.14":{"date":"07\/13\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The login, registration, and profile pages now render inside the theme layout instead of showing just a heading with no form\n"},"2.1.13":{"date":"07\/08\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added a `tailwind4:` contract to the theme config, so the [Tailwind4 plugin](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-plugin-tailwind4) can compile the theme's CSS from PHP with no Node\/npm toolchain. The npm build scripts still work; both produce the same output\n"},"2.1.12":{"date":"07\/06\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the documentation version (sidebar navigation and version badge) being misdetected on any page that is the configured `system.home.alias`. Grav collapses such a page's `route()` to `\/`, which hid the version prefix and forced a fall-through to `default_version` \u2014 so with a non-default `default_version`, pages under another version rendered the default version's navigation and badge. Version detection now reads `rawRoute()`, which always carries the real `\/<version>\/...` path\n"},"2.1.11":{"date":"07\/05\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed wide tables no longer scrolling horizontally on narrow screens\/mobile. Content tables are now their own horizontal scroll container (`display:block` with `overflow-x:auto`), so oversized tables scroll instead of squishing while narrow tables still fill the full content width [#599](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/599)\n"},"2.1.10":{"date":"07\/01\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the `[doc-image]` lightbox opening the raw image file instead of the zoom overlay. The 2.1.9 fix for #598 added a capture-phase click guard that stopped propagation on any link to a media file, which fired before the lightbox link's own bubble-phase handler could `preventDefault()`. The guard now leaves `hx-boost=\"false\"` links (including the lightbox link) alone, since HTMX never boosts them anyway [#598](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/598)\n"},"2.1.9":{"date":"06\/30\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed HTMX navigation hijacking links to media files, so clicking a local PDF or other attachment now opens it in the browser instead of dumping its contents into the page [#598](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/598)\n"},"2.1.8":{"date":"06\/18\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Hardened HTMX back\/forward navigation against browser-specific history failures (notably Brave, where Shields can partition or clear `localStorage` and leave htmx's history snapshot cache empty). Set `htmx-config` `refreshOnHistoryMiss: true` so a history cache miss falls back to a full page reload instead of a silent AJAX swap that could update the URL without updating the content [#594](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/594)\n"},"2.1.7":{"date":"06\/16\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the back\/forward button losing the page chrome (sidebar, header, TOC) during HTMX-boosted navigation. On a history cache miss htmx re-fetches the URL and replaces the whole `<body>`, but the theme only checked for the `HX-Request` header and returned the chrome-less content partial. It now excludes history-restore requests (`HX-History-Restore-Request`) so the back button receives the full page. Also added `Vary: HX-Request, HX-History-Restore-Request` so Grav's long `Cache-Control` can't let a cached partial poison a later full navigation\n"},"2.1.6":{"date":"06\/14\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the left navigation menu and version switcher not showing when Helios was used as a custom copy or inherited child theme [#592](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/592)\n"},"2.1.5":{"date":"06\/04\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed a fatal `Unknown \"native_name\" function` Twig error that took down the whole site when Helios was used without the Langswitcher plugin installed. The header partials included `partials\/langswitcher.html.twig` unconditionally, and although the partial guards its body with `{% if langswitcher is defined %}`, Twig still parses the `native_name()` call at compile time and throws because the function is only registered by the Langswitcher plugin. Wrapped the `{% include %}` in `header.html.twig` and `header-simple.html.twig` with `{% if langswitcher is defined %}` so the partial is never compiled when the plugin is absent\n"},"2.1.4":{"date":"05\/26\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `[doc-steps]` rendering the native `<ol>` decimal marker alongside the custom step-number badge. The `.prose ol` rule was overriding `.doc-steps`'s `list-none` due to higher selector specificity; qualified the selector as `ol.doc-steps` so the list marker stays suppressed inside prose content [#584](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/584)\n"},"2.1.3":{"date":"05\/20\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `[doc-image]` rendering as a broken image when `src` referenced a page-local file (e.g. `feathers-mcgraw.webp`), a `..\/`-relative path, or a Grav stream (`theme:\/\/`, `user:\/\/`, `image:\/\/`). The shortcode now resolves `src` through Grav's standard path resolution (`Excerpts::processLinkHtml`), matching how markdown image paths are handled, while deliberately bypassing the Medium image pipeline so animated GIFs and animated WebPs stay animated [#581](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/581)\n    * Fixed `[doc-image]` lightbox issues with animated GIFs (and other images): clicking a lightbox image inside the HTMX-boosted main region was being intercepted by `hx-boost`, causing the page to AJAX-navigate to the raw image URL. The lightbox link now opts out of boost. Also fixed the close button being un-clickable when the click landed on the inner SVG strokes [#581](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/581)\n    "},"2.1.2":{"date":"05\/19\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Reworked content-width model so `navigation.content_width` now represents the total content area (article plus the TOC slot). The article automatically fills the freed-up space when the TOC is hidden, instead of leaving a fixed gap. Default bumped from `768` to `1040` so existing reading widths stay the same when the TOC is visible; allowed range widened to `800`\u2013`1600`.\n    * Existing configs with a saved `content_width` below `900` are auto-promoted to the new total-width interpretation, so older sites keep rendering at the same article width without manual changes.\n    * Unified the regular Twig and HTMX render paths into a single `partials\/swap-body.html.twig` partial \u2014 both full page loads and HTMX swaps now produce identical inner HTML by construction, preventing future drift between the two. Per-template files (`doc`, `chapter`, `api-endpoint`, `api-collection`, `error`) collapsed to extends-only since the shared partial handles template dispatch.\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed HTMX navigation rendering the article at the wrong width after the content-width rework. The width rule now lives in Twig and is shipped to the client via `htmx-nav-state`, so the JS no longer re-derives it.\n    * Fixed `navigation.content_when_toc_hidden: contained` being ignored on HTMX-navigated pages (the JS was always treating TOC-hidden as expand-content).\n    * Fixed pages without any qualifying TOC headings (e.g. pages with just an H1) rendering the article at the narrower with-TOC width on full page loads, while HTMX swaps to the same page rendered correctly at the expanded width. `base.html.twig` now pre-renders the TOC partial and checks whether it produced any content, applying the same expand-when-empty rule the HTMX JS already used.\n    * Fixed `[doc-image]` lightbox issues with animated GIFs (and other images): clicking a lightbox image inside the HTMX-boosted main region was being intercepted by `hx-boost`, causing the page to AJAX-navigate to the raw image URL. The lightbox link now opts out of boost. Also fixed the close button being un-clickable when the click landed on the inner SVG strokes [#581](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/581)\n"},"2.1.1":{"date":"04\/24\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added `navigation.content_when_toc_hidden` theme option (`full` | `contained`) controlling how content is laid out when the on-page TOC is hidden. Default `full` expands content into the reserved TOC space so the content's horizontal position stays the same as pages that have a TOC (no layout jump). `contained` keeps the content at its configured width, leaving a blank gutter where the TOC would be. Overridable per page via `navigation.content_when_toc_hidden` in page frontmatter.\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `#toc-layout` collapsing to `max-content` on short pages, causing the content to appear as a narrow centered column instead of filling the configured content width [#566](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/566)\n    * Fixed breadcrumb walker pushing Grav's internal pages root node, producing a stray \"Pages\" crumb between the home icon and the current page title on any top-level non-home page [#567](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/567)\n    * Fixed breadcrumb \"home\" link and version-switcher fallback URL dropping the multisite environment prefix on subfolder installs that use Grav's `setup.php` multi-site pattern [#565](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/565)\n"},"2.1.0":{"date":"04\/24\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added a new **collection** style API format that works well for large API documentation as it bundles an entire endpoint (POST\/PUT\/GET\/PATCH\/DELETE, etc) into a single page.\n"},"2.0.5":{"date":"03\/06\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added language switcher dropdown in the header when the `langswitcher` plugin is active and multiple languages are configured. Displays languages in their native names with a compact globe-icon trigger.\n"},"2.0.4":{"date":"03\/06\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n  * Added a simple 'extends' tempalte for `docs.html.twig` to extend the Helios provided `doc.html.twig` template\n1. [](#bugfix)\n   * Added a check for yetisearch-pro's branding toggle in Helios' template override\n"}}},"quark-a11y":{"name":"Quark-A11y","version":"1.2.0","description":"Quark theme with accessibility improvements","description_html":"<p>Quark theme with accessibility improvements<\/p>","description_plain":"Quark theme with accessibility improvements","icon":"microchip","author":{"name":"Pedro Moreno","url":"https:\/\/pmdesign.dev","email":"pmoreno@pmdesign.dev"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.8"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-quark-a11y","docs":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-quark-a11y\/blob\/main\/README.md","demo":"https:\/\/quark-a11y.pmdesign.dev\/","keywords":"quark, spectre, theme, core, modern, fast, responsive, html5, css3, accessibility, semantic","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-quark-a11y\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"1.2.0","date":"2026-07-06T15:36:34Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/quark-a11y\/1.2.0","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-quark-a11y","slug":"quark-a11y","install_path":"user\/themes\/quark-a11y","content_sha256":"f5f35a6271992a15a0c917ff18ad8b3c5ae4db134c5208522a21ede760317fd6","screenshot":"themes-quark-a11y.jpg","changelog":{"1.2.0":{"date":" 07\/06\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Enhanced keyboard navigation for mobile menu toggle (Enter and Space keys)\n    * Improved aria-expanded state management for menu accessibility\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Full Grav 2.0 compatibility while maintaining Grav 1.7 support\n    * Modernized PHP code with return type hints (PHP 8.3 compatible)\n    * Replaced Elvis operator (`?:`) with null-coalescing operator (`??`) in some Twig templates\n    * Updated Twig template syntax for Twig 3 compatibility\n    * Display Grav and theme version info in footer\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed popular tags not displaying on blog item pages\n    * Fixed sidebar variable passing in item template for proper context inheritance\n    * Fixed taxonomy list validation to handle undefined page context gracefully\n"},"1.1.2":{"date":" 11\/01\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Standardized Twig template formatting using [CS fixer tool](https:\/\/github.com\/VincentLanglet\/Twig-CS-Fixer)\n"},"1.1.1":{"date":" 10\/21\/2025","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Added missing `_labels.scss` partial to `theme.scss`\n"},"1.1.0":{"date":" 10\/21\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Added bottom border to links for better accessibility\n    * Improved color contrast for better readability\n    * Separated layout and classes in features configuration\n    * Added class field to text template blueprint\n"},"1.0.0":{"date":" 09\/04\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started..."}}},"akazie-forest":{"name":"Akazie Forest","version":"0.2.2","description":"A Forest Theme","description_html":"<p>A Forest Theme<\/p>","description_plain":"A Forest Theme","icon":"rebel","author":{"name":"Tamara","email":"support@akazie.com"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/AkazieIT\/grav-theme-akazie-forest","demo":"https:\/\/demo.akazie.com\/akazie-forest\/","keywords":"grav, theme, etc","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/AkazieIT\/grav-theme-akazie-forest\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"0.2.2","date":"2026-08-25T10:34:17Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/akazie-forest\/0.2.2","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/AkazieIT\/grav-theme-akazie-forest","slug":"akazie-forest","install_path":"user\/themes\/akazie-forest","content_sha256":"08bcbfe4a37e1e86b16fa11ea1aced4f34a85dc9afb5e86ad2aeb07d0a0a31c8","screenshot":"themes-akazie-forest.jpg","changelog":{"0.1.41":{"date":" 05\/15\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Initial publication: first release of Akazie Forest in the Grav Package Manager\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Colours consolidated into CSS variables (`--tertiaryDark`, `--white`, `--teamMemberOverlay`, \u2026); the hard-coded hex values scattered through buttons, backgrounds and overlays now reference them, so a colour change no longer has to be made in several places\n    * Hero: added a bottom margin that grows on wide screens (from 1400px up), and gave the hero wrapper its own module id class so hero-specific styles no longer leak into other modules\n"},"0.1.0":{"date":" 08\/17\/2023","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started..."}}},"delivernext":{"name":"DeliverNext","version":"2.4.0","description":"DeliverNext theme is a port of the original Deliver Grav theme.","description_html":"<p>DeliverNext theme is a port of the original Deliver Grav theme.<\/p>","description_plain":"DeliverNext theme is a port of the original Deliver Grav theme.","icon":"newspaper-o","author":{"name":"Pedro Moreno","email":"pmoreno@pmdesign.dev"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.49.5"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-delivernext","docs":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-delivernext\/blob\/main\/README.md","demo":"https:\/\/delivernext.pmdesign.dev\/","keywords":"deliver, theme, modern, fast, responsive, html5, css3","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-delivernext\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"2.4.0","date":"2026-07-24T22:04:56Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/delivernext\/2.4.0","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-theme-delivernext","slug":"delivernext","install_path":"user\/themes\/delivernext","content_sha256":"b12d3931f2d80e871bf0d7618b7f705a39c2846b2c596102f972fb35cbe9cf1b","screenshot":"themes-delivernext.jpg","changelog":{"2.4.0":{"date":"07\/24\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added Intl plugin integration for localized date formatting across theme (dates, archives, etc)\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Improved featured posts mobile responsive layout\n"},"2.3.1":{"date":"07\/21\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed Featured Posts widget to ensure Grav 1.7 compatibility by removing Twig 3-specific functions and null coalescing operators\n"},"2.3.0":{"date":"07\/21\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added Featured Posts widget to blog sidebar - displays highlighted articles based on `featured: true` flag in post frontmatter\n    * Added `featured` toggle field to blog item blueprint for marking posts as featured\n    * Added dedicated Blog configuration tab in theme settings with sidebar customization options\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Enhanced Taxonomy List with optional `filterend` parameter to limit displayed tags\/categories per page\n    * Optimized featured posts and related pages CSS using SCSS mixins to reduce code duplication\n    * Translation keys restructured for better organization under `DELIVERNEXT.ADMIN.THEME.BLOG` namespace\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed Team module grid alignment. Ensured consistent column width calculation across all breakpoints using calc()\n    * Fixed range field min\/max validation in Grav 2.x by using field-level properties instead of validate section\n"},"2.2.0":{"date":"07\/17\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added `item_external_url` and `item_external_text` fields to Item blueprint for external links (original articles, reposts, etc.)\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Removed incorrect `markdown: true` configuration from `header.module_classes` field in all modular blueprints - this field contains only CSS class names and does not require markdown processing\n    * Updated summary field help text in all languages to clearly document the new behavior\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed Team template member description field not being processed as Markdown by adding `|markdown` filter\n    * Fixed Blog summary configuration to properly separate concerns between blog listing and individual article pages\n"},"2.1.2":{"date":"07\/10\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Added `latin-ext` subset to Google Fonts imports to support special characters like \u0117, \u0173, \u00c4, \u00d6, \u00dc\n    * Added `content-wrapper` div to modular_alt, error, and gallery templates for proper content margins\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed favicon type attribute not being rendered correctly by using proper object access to `favicon_data.type`\n    * Fixed `show_title` option not being respected in default, blog, archive, modular_alt, and item templates\n"},"2.1.1":{"date":"07\/09\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added `ICON_HELP` translation for social media icons field in all languages\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Changed `IMAGE_TITLE` to `TITLE` in GALLERY section of `en.yaml`\n    "},"2.1.0":{"date":"07\/09\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added French language. Thanks to ([@StudioDanton](https:\/\/github.com\/StudioDanton\/))\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Added improved handling of quicklink.url in the footer\n    * Fixed wrong variable and missing new target for gps location in footer. Thanks to ([@StudioDanton](https:\/\/github.com\/StudioDanton\/))\n    * Fixed custom css and js activation and remove them from admin mode. Thanks to ([@StudioDanton](https:\/\/github.com\/StudioDanton\/))\n    * Added new `use-minified-css` configuration option with explicit fallback to `production-mode`\n    * Fixed missing author field inside blog item admin page. Thanks to ([@StudioDanton](https:\/\/github.com\/StudioDanton\/))\n    * Fixed double-escaping in meta_description by removing contradictory\n    * Refactored JSON-LD schema generation to use json_encode() for proper\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * Removed dependency on translate-date and twig-extensions plugins\n"},"2.0.0":{"date":"07\/07\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Dual compatibility: Full support for Grav 1.7 and Grav 2.0\n\n2. [](#improved)\n    * **Twig 3 modernization**:\n    - Replaced deprecated `|defined` filter with Twig 3-compatible null-safe patterns\n    - Updated Elvis operator `?:` to null-coalesce operator `??` for consistency\n    - Normalized featured image handling: supports both `featured_image` and `featuredImage` header keys\n    - Added `ignore missing` to template includes for enhanced robustness\n    * **Blueprint modernization**:\n    - Updated all page blueprints: changed `'@extends'` to `extends@` syntax (Grav 2.x native)\n    - Normalized blueprint structure for consistency (formdata.yaml and 8 modular templates)\n    * **Social media icon field refactor**:\n    - Changed social media icon field from `iconpicker` to `text` type with flexible input formats\n    - Added icon format normalization in template: accepts \"facebook\", \"fa-facebook\", or \"fa fa-facebook\" formats\n    * **PHP 8.3 compatibility**:\n    - Added explicit return type hints (`:void`) to event handler methods\n    - Removed unused imports and legacy code\n    * **Admin simplification**:\n    - Removed `\/admin\/themes\/grav\/` customizations (no longer needed in Grav 2.x)\n    - Theme now uses core Admin defaults for both Grav 1.7 and Grav 2.x\n"},"1.4.3":{"date":"11\/11\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Set the dependency for the Grav version to 1.7.49.5\n"},"1.4.2":{"date":"09\/28\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Improved thumbnail logic to prefer local images and fallback to title in gallery template\n    * Improved styles for footer social icons and form buttons\n    * Updated demo pages\n"},"1.4.1":{"date":"07\/26\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * **Fixed**: Added missing Slide effect to the transition options in the Showcase template\n"},"1.4.0":{"date":"07\/16\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added support in the Showcase template for displaying slides in fullscreen mode\n    * Added lazy-loading support for images in the Showcase template\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Updated features styling: equal height blocks, centered icons, hover shadow, and consistent spacing\n    * Optimized styles and asset loading to improve Lighthouse performance\n    * Updated `features.md` demo page\n"},"1.3.1":{"date":"06\/30\/2025","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed thumbnail display issue for local videos by changing `videoItem.thumbnail` to `videoItem.local_thumbnail` in gallery template\n"},"1.3.0":{"date":"06\/29\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * New modular template for image galleries, featuring [GLightbox JS](https:\/\/biati-digital.github.io\/glightbox\/) integration\u2014responsive, lightweight, and customizable, with native support for both local videos (MP4\/WebM\/OGV) and embedded content (YouTube\/Vimeo).\n"},"1.2.0":{"date":"06\/21\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Removed **Bourbon Sass** dependency and all related imports\/mixins from SCSS files\n    * Removed **Color-Schemer** functionality from Sass files\n    * Removed all references to **Pure CSS** framework throughout the theme\n    * Enhanced CSS classes for better styling and functionality in the theme's admin panel\n    * Restructured all SCSS files that previously relied on Bourbon, implementing native Sass solutions where needed\n"},"1.1.2":{"date":"06\/04\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Added `archives.yaml` to demo content\n    * Added demo page and extra documentation links to README \n"},"1.1.1":{"date":"03\/27\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Added `blog_url` variable to Archives blueprint \n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed taxonomy and archives link paths in Archive template\n"},"1.1.0":{"date":"03\/27\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * New RelatedPages template for blog pages\n    * Added sidebar widget text in blueprints\n    * Added dynamic listing titles based on URL parameters (category, tag, author, archives_month) in blog template\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Updated translations\n    * Refactored code for the Sidebar\n    * Fixed featured image size in blog articles\n    * Updated `item.html.twig` to pass `big_header` dynamically\n"},"1.0.1":{"date":"03\/20\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added demo content\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `z-index` in back-to-top button\n"},"1.0.0":{"date":"03\/18\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started..."}}},"hadron":{"name":"Hadron","version":"3.0.0","description":"Hadron is more than a modern and customizable Grav theme and skeleton. On the one hand, it is optimized for beginners to quickly create a simple website, but on the other hand, it is also suitable for professionals who want to use Hadron as a foundation for a complex website with self-developed functions.","description_html":"<p>Hadron is more than a modern and customizable Grav theme and skeleton. On the one hand, it is optimized for beginners to quickly create a simple website, but on the other hand, it is also suitable for professionals who want to use Hadron as a foundation for a complex website with self-developed functions.<\/p>","description_plain":"Hadron is more than a modern and customizable Grav theme and skeleton. On the one hand, it is optimized for beginners to quickly create a simple website, but on the other hand, it is also suitable for professionals who want to use Hadron as a foundation for a complex website with self-developed functions.","icon":"circle","author":{"name":"Crabston GmbH","url":"https:\/\/crabston.dev","email":"contact@crabston.dev"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=2.0.0"},{"name":"quark2","version":">=1.0.0"}],"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/Crabston\/grav-t