26","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Restored the social field name in the blueprint for admin compatibility\n    "},"3.6.0":{"date":"04\/24\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added floating social icons feature: configurable floating icons for social media, with new blueprint section and backward compatibility for previous social list configuration.\n"},"3.5.0":{"date":"03\/14\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Hierarchical subpage index: show child pages as a structured, numbered index (configurable depth)\n"},"3.4.0":{"date":"02\/24\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added page index option to default template blueprint and translations\n"},"3.3.0":{"date":"02\/22\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Improved TOC rendering logic and inline TOC support to avoid empty containers\n    * Replaced `header_var()` usage with explicit `page.header.*` access in theme templates\n    * Unified default values between blueprints and Twig templates\n    * Updated translations and added shadow effect to box styles\n"},"3.2.1":{"date":"02\/05\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Completed Deutsch translations for blog share icon labels\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Added LinkedIn share icon checkbox for item pages\n"},"3.2.0":{"date":"02\/03\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added new modular \"text\" template with flexible layouts (1, 2, or 3 columns) and box classes\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Improved contact template functionality\n    * Enhanced banner and features templates for improved design and presentation\n    * Fixed logo.html.twig to allow users to disable the default logo display\n    * Enhanced SCSS styles for boxes, including button positioning, link styling, and other improvements\n    * Updated translations for new features\n    * Updated demo content to showcase new text template with various box styles\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed URL encoding issue in footer button link to properly support anchor URLs like '#'\n"},"3.1.0":{"date":"12\/29\/2025","content":"1.  [](#new)\n    * French translation added (thanks to [em3link](https:\/\/github.com\/em3link))\n2.  [](#improved)\n    * Twig `same as` syntax fixed for Grav 1.8 compatibility\n    * Responsive breakpoint for sidebar menu updated\n"},"3.0.0":{"date":"11\/13\/2025","content":"1.  [](#improved)\n    * Improved `blog.html.twig` template for better featured image handling\n    * Language translation files have been organized separately by language in the `languages` folder for improved maintainability\n    * Pass `featured_image` and `show_image` as parameters to blog_item partial template\n    * **Important Change:** Since version 1.2.1, `featured_image` is the primary field for page images. Existing pages using `primaryImage` will continue to work, but please update your frontmatter to `featured_image` for consistency.\n"},"2.2.3":{"date":"11\/11\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * Downgraded Grav version dependency from 1.7.50 to 1.7.49.5\n"},"2.2.2":{"date":"10\/29\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * `social_style` has been added to the social icon options in the theme settings\n   * Standardized Twig template formatting using [CS fixer tool](https:\/\/github.com\/VincentLanglet\/Twig-CS-Fixer)\n"},"2.2.1":{"date":"10\/23\/2025","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n   * Fixed Twig template loading by adding `onTwigLoader` event to `getSubscribedEvents`\n"},"2.2.0":{"date":"10\/15\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * Refactored `metadata.html.twig` with organized structure, optimized SEO metadata generation, and removed redundant conditionals\n   * Migrated all SCSS code to modern Sass syntax (Dart Sass)\n   * **Twig Templates**: Updated output filtering practices following security best practices\n   * Refactored `onTwigSiteVariables()` to dynamically detect active theme\n   * **Changed:** Plugin dependencies are no longer automatically installed. They are now listed as recommendations in the README for manual installation and greater user control.\n   * **Refactored:** Theme configuration blueprint has been modularized into separate files (`header.yaml`, `footer.yaml`, etc.) for improved organization and maintainability.\n"}}},"afterblog":{"name":"Afterblog","version":"0.9.0","description":"Afterblog is modern, responsive, and **built for speed**!","description_html":"<p>Afterblog is modern, responsive, and <strong>built for speed<\/strong>!<\/p>","description_plain":"Afterblog is modern, responsive, and built for speed!","icon":"barcode","author":{"name":"Andrea ZH Rustichelli","url":"http:\/\/www.andrea.rustichelli.name\/demo-grav-theme-afterblog","email":"andrea@andrea.rustichelli.name"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.5.10"}],"keywords":"afterblog, blog, theme, modern, fast, responsive","license":"MIT","tag_name":"v0.9.0","date":"2021-09-27T13:47:59Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/afterblog\/0.9.0","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/andreaZHrustichelli\/theme4grav-afterblog","homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/andreaZHrustichelli\/theme4grav-afterblog","slug":"afterblog","install_path":"user\/themes\/afterblog","content_sha256":"c5b18b2002ab3416d6d60d78c451add288f92436aba4c4d320c86ca9dcfa3aac","screenshot":"themes-afterblog.jpg","changelog":{"0.9.0":{"date":"2021-09-16","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added support for *Reading Time* plugin\n    * Blog show only first *N* post, then show the 'short' version\n    * Add some CSS style in file *afterblog.css*\n    * Add default value for fields in *blueprints.yaml*\n1. [](#improved)\n    * In page *blog_item_shot.html.twig* added section based on *Taxonomy List* plugin status\n    * In page *blog_item.html.twig* added section based on *Taxonomy List* plugin status\n1. [](#change)\n    * The rusults of *SimpleSearch* is shown only with *blog_item_shot.html.twig*\n    * Customized some graphic elements of the page *About* in the *afterblog.css* file\n    * Rename some classes within the file *info_bar.html.twig*\n1. [](#remove)\n    * Message for internet errors in *blueprints.yaml*\n"},"0.8.0":{"date":"11\/08\/2021","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started..."}}},"typhoon":{"name":"Typhoon","version":"4.3.10","description":"Typhoon theme utilizing the NEW Tailwind 4.1 CSS framework","description_html":"<p>Typhoon theme utilizing the NEW Tailwind 4.1 CSS framework<\/p>","description_plain":"Typhoon theme utilizing the NEW Tailwind 4.1 CSS framework","icon":"bolt","author":{"name":"Trilby Media, LLC","email":"hello@trilby.media"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.6"},{"name":"color-tools","version":">=1.1.1"},{"name":"svg-icons","version":">=1.0.0"},{"name":"shortcode-core","version":">=4.0.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/typhoon","docs":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/typhoon\/docs","demo":"https:\/\/demo.getgrav.org\/typhoon\/","keywords":"grav, theme, tailwind, responsive, modern, premium","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/labels\/typhoon","license":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/license","tag_name":"4.3.10","date":"2026-08-11T19:22:27Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/themes\/typhoon\/4.3.10","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/trilbymedia\/grav-theme-typhoon","premium":{"permalink":"grav-premium-typhoon","validator":"local","checkout_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/premium\/typhoon","button":"Buy Now","filename":"grav-theme-typhoon"},"slug":"typhoon","install_path":"user\/themes\/typhoon","content_sha256":"4a6f5812015bd5a0f4d0821240984a03ddbb06b69b6a296ed8950d173e285112","screenshot":"themes-typhoon.jpg","changelog":{"4.3.10":{"date":"08\/11\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * The Wrapper Classes setting now explains that only classes already compiled into the shipped stylesheet take effect, and which ones those are.\n"},"4.3.9":{"date":"07\/31\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Form fields no longer show their dark-mode colours while the site is in light mode.\n1. [](#improved)\n    * The compiled stylesheet is now generated by the tailwind4 plugin, so it stays in step with the theme's own sources.\n"},"4.3.8":{"date":"07\/17\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Tag lists now respect an optional `filterend` limit so you can cap how many tags are shown ([#219](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-theme-quark\/issues\/219))\n"},"4.3.7":{"date":"07\/13\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added a horizontal image alignment option to the hero (left\/center\/right), complementing the existing vertical alignment so the focal point of a cropped hero image can be set on both axes ([#605](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/605))\n"},"4.3.6":{"date":"07\/08\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed typography (`prose`) styles not applying to page content, so headings, paragraphs, lists, and code in the main content area rendered unstyled. The compiled CSS shipped in 4.3.5 had the descendant combinator stripped from every prose selector (`.prose :where(h1)` became `.prose:where(h1)`, which matches nothing); the CSS has been recompiled correctly.\n"},"4.3.5":{"date":"07\/08\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added a `tailwind4:` contract to the theme config, so the [Tailwind4 plugin](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-plugin-tailwind4) can compile the theme's CSS from PHP with no Node\/npm toolchain. The npm build scripts still work; both produce the same output\n"},"4.3.4":{"date":"07\/07\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Footer social links now use the svg-icons `brands` icon set for every network, so all icons render in a single consistent badge style; legacy `<network>__brands` selections keep working ([#604](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/604))\n    * Added X, TikTok, Threads, Bluesky, Mastodon, Discord, Twitch, WhatsApp, Telegram, and Reddit to the footer social network options\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed footer social icons for YouTube and Vimeo being barely visible, and 500px and GitBook not rendering at all, caused by the brand color classes never being compiled into the theme CSS ([#604](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/604))\n    * Fixed the hero overlay gradient opacity and direction settings being ignored when set as a comma-separated value, so the two opacity stops now apply correctly ([#602](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/602))\n"},"4.3.3":{"date":"06\/25\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Declared Grav 2.0 compatibility in the theme blueprint; Typhoon now officially supports both Grav 1.7 and 2.0\n"},"4.3.2":{"date":"06\/22\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Scrollspy on-page navigation now auto-centers the active section in the bar as you scroll, so the current section stays visible on narrow screens where the bar overflows horizontally ([#595](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/595))\n    * Added \"scroll to top\" and \"scroll to bottom\" controls to the scrollspy bar\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the scrollspy bar sometimes failing to auto-hide when scrolling quickly to the top, caused by the Alpine `throttle` dropping the trailing scroll event; added a `scrollend` handler to settle the final state ([#595](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/595))\n    * Fixed the last section never highlighting when scrolled to the very bottom of the page\n"},"4.3.1":{"date":"06\/09\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Upgraded to latest Tailwind + other libraries\n    * Added user\/plugins to resolve-paths.js to fix relative path resolution for plugins\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the language switcher menu generating the wrong default-language link when `include_default_lang` is off, so switching back to the default language now works ([#591](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/591))\n    * Fixed a bogus language switcher entry appearing on the scrollspy on-page navigation bar ([#590](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/590))\n"},"4.3.0":{"date":"05\/10\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Restored `modular\/notices` blueprint and template so the multi-language notices page can be selected from the modular type dropdown again ([#577](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/577))\n1. [](#improved)\n    * Removed legacy `only_homepage` fallback from `partials\/notices.html.twig`; the `route` field has been the canonical mechanism for some time and `route: '\/'` already covers homepage-only\n"},"4.2.1":{"date":"04\/07\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * Added hreflang partial twig if `langswitcher` is available.\n"},"4.2.0":{"date":"03\/06\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added new scrollspy on-page navigation mode for modular pages. When `onpage_menu` is enabled with `onpage_menu_replace: false`, a sticky scrollspy bar slides into view as you scroll, highlighting the active section \u2014 while keeping the main navigation intact\n    * Added `Replace Main Menu` toggle to modular page blueprint to choose between legacy menu-replacement behavior (default) and the new scrollspy bar\n    * Added symlink-aware `resolve-sources.js` script for Tailwind CSS builds, ensuring correct `@source` paths when the theme is symlinked during development\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed empty fixed header bar appearing on mobile when `Display Mobile Navigation` is disabled and `Fixed Header Bar` is enabled ([#548](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/548))\n    * Fixed FOUC (flash of unstyled content) on page load by adding inline early theme-detection script\n1. [](#improved)\n    * Updated to latest Tailwind `v4.2.1`\n"},"4.1.0":{"date":"11\/12\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Updated to latest Tailwind `v4.1.17`\n"},"4.0.4":{"date":"03\/17\/2025","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed invalid nesting in `sidebar-nav` styling\n"},"4.0.3":{"date":"03\/14\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Updated to latest Tailwind `v4.0.14`\n    * UPdated AlpineJS to `3.14.9`\n"},"4.0.2":{"date":"03\/03\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Updated to latest Tailwind `v4.0.9`\n    * Minor improvements to login styling in dark mode\n"},"4.0.0":{"date":"02\/12\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n   * MAJOR UPDATE: Migrated to TailwindCSS 4.0.6\n   * HUGE SPEED INCREASES with new LightningCSS engine\n   * Migrated to `site.css` based configuration, removed `tailwind.config.js`\n   * Moved to **Vite** removed **Post CSS** for Tailwind building\n   * Optimized CSS to remove unneeded styles and unified styles so that everything uses Tailwind classes across the board\n   * Migrated deprecated classes for Tailwind 4.0\n1. [](#improved)\n   * Upgrade **AlpineJS** to `3.14.8`\n   * Updated Tailwind `forms` and `typography` plugins to latest versions\n   * Removed `columns` Tailwind plugin as no longer needed\n   * Removed `debug-screens` Tailwind plugin as not compatible with Tailwind 4.0\n"},"2.4.8":{"date":"02\/04\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * Updated to latest Tailwind `v3.4.17` + PostCss `v8.4.49`\n   * Updated `parials\/taxonomylist.html.twig` to support latest updates in that plugin\n3. [](#bugfix)\n   * Fix for `modular\/image-block.html.twig` not displaying selected image correctly\n"},"2.4.7":{"date":"11\/06\/2024","content":"1. [](#improved)\n   * Added some basic login form styling (disable login's built-in CSS first) [getgrav\/grav-premium-issues#433](https:\/\/github.com\/getgrav\/grav-premium-issues\/issues\/433)\n   * Updated to latest Tailwind `v3.4.14` + other Tailwind plugins updates\n   * Added `dev` (`watch`) and `prod` (`build`) alias commands for development\n   * Support shortcodes in hero `title1` and `title2`\n3. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed an issue that was breaking `text-primary-darker` and `bg-primary-darker`\n"}}},"highlights":{"name":"Highlights","version":"1.0.3","des